%I A400940 #19 Oct 29 2026 17:35:15
%S A400940 1,2,12,13,51,125,5091,6344
%N A400940 a(1) = 1; a(k+1) is the smallest positive integer that has not appeared among the first f(a(k)) terms of A400939, where f(m) is the index of the first occurrence of m in A400939.
%C A400940 Sequence of holdouts from the Halving Recaman Sieve. Sieve description: write out the positive integers and cross off every number visited by the walk A400939. The current term is the smallest number not yet crossed off, when it is finally crossed off, the new smallest uncrossed number is the next term.
%C A400940 Equivalently, m is a term if and only if every positive integer smaller than m appears in A400939 before m does.
%C A400940 Conjecture: Sequence A400939 contains every positive integer, so this sequence is infinite.
%C A400940 Note: 6343 does not appear among the first 2*10^11 terms in A400939.
%C A400940 f(a(k)) = 1, 102, 333, 122524, 808054764, 28626066582, 111647551484 for k = 1..7.
%H A400940 Zlatko Damijanic, <a href="/A400940/a400940.txt">C program for computing the holdouts and the walk A400939</a>
%o A400940 (Python) # too slow beyond a(5)
%o A400940 def aupton(n):
%o A400940     s, p, m, out, k = {1}, 1, 2, [1, 2], 1
%o A400940     while len(out) < n:
%o A400940         k += 1
%o A400940         p = p//2 if p%2 == 0 and p//2 not in s else p+k
%o A400940         s.add(p)
%o A400940         if p == m:
%o A400940             while m in s: m += 1
%o A400940             out.append(m)
%o A400940     return out[:n]
%Y A400940 Cf. A400939, A005132.
%K A400940 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A400940 1,2
%A A400940 _Zlatko Damijanic_, Oct 10 2026
